# WARP-8: GLO held, the keys mute: a black key a drum of the kit (from any track), the first three white keys the
# kit, the sample track, the slice track; the last white key held is a fill, and a step's chance can be "fill"
wait 300
listen
expect trk 1
press GLO
tapkey b2
release GLO
wait 40
expect kmute 4
press GLO
tapkey b2
release GLO
wait 40
expect kmute 0
press GLO
tapkey w1
release GLO
wait 40
expect mute 2
press GLO
tapkey w1
release GLO
wait 40
expect mute 0
# from the sample track too: the kit's fourth drum
press HOME
turn ALGO 1
release HOME
wait 40
expect trk 2
press GLO
tapkey b3
release GLO
wait 40
expect kmute 8
press GLO
tapkey b3
release GLO
press HOME
turn ALGO -1
release HOME
wait 40
expect trk 1
expect kmute 0
# a kick on step 1, and one on step 9 that plays only in a fill
tap SEQ
tapkey b0
tapkey w0
tapkey w8
key w8 down
wait 400
turn K3 200
turn K3 -1
wait 40
key w8 up
wait 40
expect drumhits 1
tap PLAY
wait 1500
tap PLAY
expect drumhits 2
press GLO
key w15 down
wait 40
release GLO
said FILL
tap PLAY
wait 1500
tap PLAY
key w15 up
expect drumhits 4
